Apple's tech specs suggest the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a>'s Main camera sensor is seemingly a match for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17e/">iPhone 17e</a>'s, not the standard <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17/">iPhone 17</a>'s.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iphone-duo-selfie.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="899" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063435" /><br/>
According to Apple's <a href="https://www.apple.com/iphone-duo/specs/">tech specs page for the iPhone Duo</a>, the Main camera is a 26mm, ƒ/1.6 sensor with sensor-shift optical image stabilization and Hybrid Focus Pixels, also enabling a 12MP 2x Telephoto crop from the same sensor. The <a href="https://www.apple.com/iphone-17e/specs/">iPhone 17e's tech specs page</a> lists an identical 26mm, ƒ/1.6 Main camera with Hybrid Focus Pixels, the same autofocus terminology Apple uses for the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;.<br/>
<br/>
The match is not total, though. The &zwnj;iPhone 17e&zwnj;'s tech specs describes plain "optical image stabilization" with no "sensor-shift" qualifier, while the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;'s <em>does</em> include it. That detail instead lines up with the standard <a href="https://www.apple.com/iphone-17/specs/">iPhone 17's tech specs page</a>, which pairs sensor-shift OIS with a different autofocus term, "100% Focus Pixels," the wording <a href="https://www.apple.com/iphone-18-pro/specs/">iPhone 18 Pro's tech specs page</a> also uses but Duo and 17e do not.<br/>
<br/>
This suggests that the Main camera of the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; realistically falls somewhere between the &zwnj;iPhone 17e&zwnj; and &zwnj;iPhone 17&zwnj;, possessing the sensor-shift optical image stabilization of the &zwnj;iPhone 17&zwnj;, but with an iPhone 17e-style sensor that uses Hybrid Focus Pixels.<br/>
<br/>
The overlapping Focus Pixels wording with the 17e is fueling speculation online that the two devices share a sensor. Apple has not published a sensor size or pixel pitch for the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;'s Main camera, leaving the matching Focus Pixels wording as the only official link to the 17e for now.<br/>
